 "notes": "transformers trust_remote_code executes attacker-controlled Python from a model directory: AutoConfig.from_pretrained(<untrusted dir>, trust_remote_code=True) copies the custom code into the HF modules cache and executes it (get_class_in_module exec_module), after check_imports() importlib.import_module()'s every top-level module the attacker file lists (line 248). Training/serving stacks that propagate trust_remote_code from config (LLaMA-Factory, ms-swift, TRL loaders) turn 'load a model from a directory/hub' into code execution. Reproduced with the real installed transformers 4.57.1 wheel: the malicious configuration module writes the proof marker during the import performed by the pinned upstream path."
